{
  "info": {
    "name": "tubodega — API v1",
    "description": "Contrato público de tubodega (MVP solo-API). Estado: Plan 1 — registro de organización, login, /me y OpenAPI.\n\nFlujo sugerido: 1) Registrar organización → guarda orgId; 2) Login → guarda accessToken y refreshToken; 3) /me.\n\nLas variables `slug`, `email` y `password` se generan solas si están vacías (pre-request de la colección) para que cada corrida cree una organización nueva. Todo error llega como application/problem+json (RFC 9457) con `type`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`, `traceId` y `errors[]`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:3000" },
    { "key": "slug", "value": "" },
    { "key": "email", "value": "" },
    { "key": "password", "value": "correcthorse1" },
    { "key": "orgId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "accessToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "refreshToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "userId", "value": "" }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Una organización nueva por corrida: slug y correo únicos si no se fijaron a mano.",
          "if (!pm.collectionVariables.get('slug')) {",
          "  const suffix = Date.now().toString(36);",
          "  pm.collectionVariables.set('slug', `la-esquina-${suffix}`);",
          "  pm.collectionVariables.set('email', `marta-${suffix}@esquina.co`);",
          "}",
          "if (!pm.collectionVariables.get('email')) {",
          "  pm.collectionVariables.set('email', `marta-${pm.collectionVariables.get('slug')}@esquina.co`);",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "pm.test('X-Request-Id es un UUID', () => {",
          "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Request-Id')).to.match(/^[0-9a-f-]{36}$/i);",
          "});",
          "if (pm.response.code >= 400) {",
          "  pm.test('los errores son application/problem+json', () => {",
          "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type')).to.include('application/problem+json');",
          "    const p = pm.response.json();",
          "    pm.expect(p).to.include.keys('type', 'title', 'status', 'detail', 'instance', 'traceId');",
          "    pm.expect(p.traceId).to.eql(pm.response.headers.get('X-Request-Id'));",
          "  });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Organizaciones",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Registrar organización",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created con Location', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Location')).to.match(/^\\/v1\\/organizations\\//);",
                  "});",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('orgId', body.organization.id);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', body.owner.id);",
                  "pm.test('el owner tiene el rol OWNER', () => pm.expect(body.owner.roles).to.eql(['OWNER']));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/organizations", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["v1", "organizations"] },
            "description": "Registro público. Crea la organización y su primer OWNER en una sola transacción. Exento de Idempotency-Key (spec 07 §5). Errores: 400 validation-failed, 409 slug-taken, 422 invalid-slug / invalid-email.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Distribuidora La Esquina\",\n  \"slug\": \"{{slug}}\",\n  \"owner\": {\n    \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n    \"name\": \"Marta\",\n    \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n  }\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Autenticación",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 con par de tokens', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(b.accessToken).to.be.a('string');",
                  "  pm.expect(b.refreshToken).to.be.a('string');",
                  "  pm.expect(b.expiresIn).to.eql(900);",
                  "});",
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', b.accessToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', b.refreshToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', b.user.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["v1", "auth", "login"] },
            "description": "Devuelve accessToken (JWT HS256, 15 min) y refreshToken (opaco, 30 días; se rota en cada uso). `slug` es opcional: obligatorio solo si el correo existe en varias organizaciones (409 ambiguous-login). Correo inexistente, contraseña errónea y usuario inactivo responden lo mismo: 401 invalid-credentials.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login con slug (correo en varias organizaciones)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["v1", "auth", "login"] },
            "description": "La misma persona puede pertenecer a dos negocios (T-1 es por organización). Sin `slug` el login es 409 ambiguous-login; con `slug` resuelve.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\",\n  \"slug\": \"{{slug}}\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Perfil",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Mi usuario y organización",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 con usuario y organización', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(b.user.id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('userId'));",
                  "  pm.expect(b.organization.id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('orgId'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/me", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["v1", "me"] },
            "description": "Requiere Bearer. Los roles vienen de la base de datos, no del token: desactivar un usuario o retirarle un rol surte efecto en la siguiente petición (T-6). Errores: 401 invalid-credentials (sin token, token inválido o usuario inactivo), 401 token-expired."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Contrato",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "OpenAPI (JSON)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('documento OpenAPI con las rutas v1', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  const paths = Object.keys(pm.response.json().paths);",
                  "  pm.expect(paths).to.include.members(['/v1/organizations', '/v1/auth/login', '/v1/me']);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/openapi.json", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["v1", "openapi.json"] },
            "description": "El contrato generado desde el código (spec 03 §10). Público."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Casos de error (para ver problem+json)",
      "description": "Peticiones que fallan a propósito. Cada una demuestra la forma RFC 9457 y un `type` estable del contrato.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "409 slug-taken — registrar el mismo slug otra vez",
          "event": [
            { "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
              "pm.test('409 slug-taken', () => {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(409);",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().type).to.eql('https://tubodega.app/errors/slug-taken');",
              "});"
            ] } }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/organizations", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["v1", "organizations"] },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Otra\",\n  \"slug\": \"{{slug}}\",\n  \"owner\": { \"email\": \"otra@esquina.co\", \"name\": \"Otra\", \"password\": \"{{password}}\" }\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "400 validation-failed — cuerpo inválido con pointers",
          "event": [
            { "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
              "pm.test('400 con errors[].pointer', () => {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
              "  const p = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect(p.type).to.eql('https://tubodega.app/errors/validation-failed');",
              "  pm.expect(p.errors.map(e => e.pointer)).to.include('/owner/password');",
              "});"
            ] } }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/organizations", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["v1", "organizations"] },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"X\",\n  \"slug\": \"La Esquina\",\n  \"owner\": { \"email\": \"a@b.co\", \"name\": \"A\" }\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "401 invalid-credentials — contraseña errónea",
          "event": [
            { "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
              "pm.test('401 invalid-credentials', () => {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().type).to.eql('https://tubodega.app/errors/invalid-credentials');",
              "});"
            ] } }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["v1", "auth", "login"] },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"nope-nope-nope\"\n}",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "401 invalid-credentials — /me sin token",
          "event": [
            { "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
              "pm.test('401 sin token', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
            ] } }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/me", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["v1", "me"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "404 not-found — ruta inexistente",
          "event": [
            { "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
              "pm.test('404 not-found en problem+json', () => {",
              "  pm.response.to.have.status(404);",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().type).to.eql('https://tubodega.app/errors/not-found');",
              "});"
            ] } }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/nope", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["v1", "nope"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "X-Request-Id — se respeta si es UUID, se sustituye si no",
          "event": [
            { "listen": "test", "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": [
              "pm.test('req-123 no es UUID: la respuesta trae uno nuevo', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('X-Request-Id')).to.not.eql('req-123');",
              "});"
            ] } }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}" },
              { "key": "X-Request-Id", "value": "req-123" }
            ],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/me", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["v1", "me"] }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
